 "narrative": [
  "The BS degree in structural engineering requires a minimum of 145 units, plus college requirements in humanities and social sciences.",
  "To graduate, students must maintain an overall GPA of at least 2.0, and the department requires at least a C– grade in each course required for the major. All courses required for the major must be taken for a letter grade.",
  "Structural engineering is a screened major. Screening courses for admitted first-year students: MATH 20A-B-C-D, MATH 18, PHYS 2A, SE 101A; for admitted transfer students: MATH 20A-B-C-D, MATH 18, PHYS 2A-B-C, SE 101A (C– or above, overall UC San Diego GPA of 2.0 or above).",
  "SE 1, SE 3, and SE 9 must be taken by all students majoring in structural engineering. Transfer students who have successfully petitioned to use a course equivalent to SE 101A prior to entering UC San Diego may take an additional technical elective in place of SE 1.",
  "Course requirements are taken from the department's curriculum table (core courses, focus sequence FS, capstone, technical electives TE).",
  "Students in the structural engineering major SE-BS-003 can choose any of the focus sequences and the corresponding capstone course(s).",
  "Geotechnical focus: SE 151A has SE 103 as a prerequisite, and SE 140A has SE 150A as a prerequisite. Students should plan to take SE 103 and SE 150A as TE classes their junior year."
 ]
